text:
 @HunterTracks  TSMC themselves list 4nm as mainstream and targets it towards cost-effective devices. Costs drop further, the longer the process is in use.

With N2 being right around the corner, tech based on 5nm/4nm is becoming more and more accessible.

8GB of GDDR6 is currently at an 18USD parts price at the spot market and has already been on that level once before - Sep. 2024. If anything, it should ultimately become even cheaper, as demand goes down.
